What you are objecting to in objectivism is Rand's nutty quirks as
amplifyed by her belief that she was hyperrational. The smoking, the
purges, the silly epistemology. Those, however, are easily discarded.
What you are left with is a very nice philosophy of life.

Small-o objectivism has helped me enormously. I am not a whining
immature brat, either, although some would occassionally accuse me of
being prematurely curmudgeonly. :-)

